  "details": "I couldn't find any documentation on it right now, but here is a article showing how that'd look like and how to use it: https://va.lent.in/unity-make-your-lists-functional-with-reorderablelist/\nMaybe it has a different name nowadays, which would explain why I couldn't find it, dunno..\nBut would definetely make the VRCExpressionParameters nicer. (could probably be used in other places like the Menu assets aswell, dunno how flexible it is overall)\n\n\nI assume VRCExpressionParameters has 16 individual properties with the name of `parameter1`, etc?... being classes / structs with `string name`, `enum type` or something along those lines. So you could just use an Array with size 16 (or more), discard the numbering and let users drag it back and forth -> first image\n\n\n\nOh and also... default value for parameters? Like they say basically: https://vrchat.canny.io/avatar-30/p/feedback-default-values-for-things-such-as-radial , just visualized that a bit in the second image attatched.",
